---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import NavBar from "../components/NavBar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Divider from "../components/Divider.astro";
---

<Layout title="ZIPTIP — NICHOLAS SOBCHAK">
  <NavBar />
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl px-6 pb-16 pt-16 md:px-10 md:pb-32 md:pt-24">
    <header class="mb-12 flex flex-col items-center gap-6 text-center">
      <img
        src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/ziptip-logo.png`}
        alt="ZipTip logo"
        width={499}
        height={504}
        class="h-48 w-48 object-contain md:h-64 md:w-64"
      />
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-gold">
        Cashless Tipping for Hospitality Workers
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://ziptip.io"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="border border-gold/60 px-5 py-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-gold transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-gold/10"
      >
        [ Visit ZipTip ]
      </a>
    </header>

    <Divider />

    <section class="mt-10">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-gold">
        [ What Is ZipTip? ]
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-academic text-lg leading-relaxed text-parchment md:text-xl">
        ZipTip is the world’s first and only cashless tipping platform built purposely for the hospitality ecosystem.
        With secure, scannable touchpoints tailored for every position, 
        rewarding great service has never been easier.<br />
        <br />
        <strong>It starts with a tap.</strong><br />
        Tippers simply scan or tap their phone to a ZipTip Touchpoint. 
        Instantly, like magic, the Service Professional’s profile appears on the screen—no clunky app downloads required.<br />
        <br />
        <strong>Then come the Tip.</strong><br />
        The guest selects from three smart, pre-set tip amounts or enters a custom gratuity of their own.<br />
        <br />
        <strong>Done.</strong><br />
        That’s it. Really. By that evening, the funds are securely deposited directly 
        into the Service Pro’s account or seamlessly routed to the Operator’s ERP for payroll. 
        Appreciation is expressed and accepted. Karma is activated. All without cash.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-gold">
        [ The Mission ]
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-academic text-lg leading-relaxed text-parchment md:text-xl">
        Hospitality workers rely on tips as a significant portion of their income,
        yet cash tipping has been declining for years. 
        Hospitality professionals miss out on $750,000,000 in tips each year because half of us don't carry cash. 
        ZipTip exists to close that gap — making tipping as easy as tapping a phone, 
        so workers get fairly compensated for the service they provide.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-gold">
        [ My Role ]
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-academic text-lg leading-relaxed text-parchment md:text-xl">
        As a Founding Software Developer, I've been involved in ZipTip since
        December 2025. I've contributed across the full stack — building and
        maintaining the backend services, to name a few — authentication &amp; authorization, 
        payment processing (stripe), managing redirects &amp; routing, meta tags, and keeping the codebase clean. 
        So far, on the frontend I help maintain the Angular web app and clean up the codebase of lint errors, AND SO ON. 

        Scan API &amp; Domain Infrastructure
        - Created the ZipTipScannables DB table and a Lambda that maps scanable IDs to tip accounts with HTTP redirects
        - Set up the ScanApiEndpoint, API Gateway, custom domain mapping for scan.ziptip.io
        - Added auth to the scan redirect flow
        Open Graph / Link Previews
        - Added OG tags for link previews with message graphics
        - Refined placard logic
        CI/CD Pipeline
        - Created and iterated on pipeline configurations
        - Fixed prod pipeline dependencies
        - Enabled rollback support
        - Added test configs and fixed boto3 credential errors
        Account Creation &amp; Auth
        - Implemented phone validation and JSON tests for AuthSignUpFunction
        - Created validators
        - Updated signup logic (username by email instead of phone)
        Merge/Housekeeping
        - Several merge commits syncing branches (nick, main, dev)
        - Removed stale folders (aws-sam, auth root folders)
        - Cleaned up linting errors

        Dev Tooling &amp; Config
        - Set up ESLint, Prettier, and Husky pre-commit tooling
        - Added a .browserslistrc targeting mobile-first browsers
        - Consolidated environment config under src/environments
        Code Quality &amp; Refactoring
        - Typed API contracts and migrated services to inject() for lint compliance — touched 28 files across components, services, guards, and interfaces
        - Fixed lint errors across several merged components (band-linking, claim-tip, dashboard, etc.)
        - Replaced synthetic identifiers in band-linking tests
        Docs &amp; Cleanup
        - Updated README and FEATURES docs to match current features
        - Removed Husky and cleaned up README
        - Fixed Amplify Node runtime and dependency lock (amplify.yml)
        Biggest piece: The inject() migration and API typing commit — that's a significant refactor touching components, services, guards, and interfaces across the app.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-academic text-lg leading-relaxed text-parchment md:text-xl">
        It's been a unique experience building a product from the ground up —
        making foundational technical decisions that will scale with the
        business, and seeing direct impact on real workers who depend on the
        platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-gold">
      [ What I've Learned ]
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-academic text-lg leading-relaxed text-parchment md:text-xl">
        Coming Soon...
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
